 ## Design system
 
-White / charcoal / gold. Components in `src/components/ui/`: `Button`,
-`Input`, `Select`, `Textarea`, `Badge`, `Avatar`, `EmptyState`, `Spinner`,
-`Modal`. Inter via Google Fonts.
+Hybrid as of the CU³ design pass: most of the app is white / charcoal /
+gold (Leads, Conversations, Knowledge, Training, Settings, Website
+Builder, Brand Studio, Hospitality). Login, Navigation (Sidebar/TopBar),
+and Dashboard use the newer CU³ treatment — dark background with a
+blue/orange radial glow (`cue-bg`), glassmorphism panels (`glass-panel`),
+gradient accents (`cue-gradient`/`cue-text`) replacing gold as primary.
+Applied module-by-module on purpose, not a global theme swap — see
+Roadmap.md. Components in `src/components/ui/`: `Button`, `Input`,
+`Select`, `Textarea`, `Badge`, `Avatar`, `EmptyState`, `Spinner`, `Modal`
+— several gained a `cue` variant or `dark` prop alongside their original
+light-theme behavior, additive, not a breaking change. Inter via Google
+Fonts.
+
+## Product principle: Compass → Revi → HASI → Execute
+
+Stated explicitly because it's easy to lose sight of once individual
+modules are being built one at a time: CUE is not trying to replace a
+business's existing CRM or operational software. It sits above those
+systems, combines their data with CUE-native data, interprets it, and
+turns that into decisions. Company Compass is where that interpretation
+surfaces (KPIs, goals, trends), Revi is what explains it to a person,
+HASI is the invisible layer that actually correlates the data across
+modules, and Execute is where an approved recommendation becomes a real
+action. Every module built against this app should be understood as
+feeding that chain eventually, not as a standalone feature competing for
+dashboard space. See Roadmap.md's Compass backlog entry for the concrete
+version of this that hasn't been scoped or built yet.
