+## Backlog: Company Compass as the intelligence layer (not yet scoped)
+
+Captured from a product-direction conversation, deliberately NOT
+scheduled and NOT started — no tables, migrations, integrations, or UI
+exist for any of this. Recorded here so the idea doesn't get lost or
+get silently half-built as a side effect of some other task.
+
+**The vision:** Company Compass becomes a real-time business intelligence
+surface — KPIs (revenue, jobs, leads, estimates, conversions,
+cancellations, cash collected, industry-specific metrics), goals with
+progress tracking, team/employee performance where relevant, and
+optional bonus/milestone tiers with progress indicators and
+celebrations. Revi explains what the numbers mean and recommends a next
+action. HASI works invisibly in the background correlating data across
+CUE's modules to detect trends, risks, and opportunities. Execute
+eventually carries out approved actions that come out of those insights.
+
+**The architectural principle worth preserving, stated precisely:**
+CUE is not trying to replace a business's CRM or operational software.
+It sits above existing systems, pulls relevant data through
+integrations, combines it with CUE-native data, interprets it, and
+turns it into decisions/actions. The distinction:
+
+- **CRM** = records what happened
+- **Dashboard** = shows what is happening
+- **CUE** = understands what it means and helps decide what should
+  happen next
+
+This is the same shape as the already-approved Growth/Scal3 boundary
+(§7 of the locked CUE Architecture Audit) — CUE doesn't replace Scal3's
+revenue intelligence, it would eventually sit above it. This backlog
+item is that same pattern applied to Company Compass specifically:
+Compass → Revi (explains) → HASI (correlates, invisibly) → Execute
+(acts, with approval) — one coherent chain, not a new one-off feature.
+
+**Before any of this gets built:** needs its own scoped conversation
+(what integrations, which KPIs are actually available from where, what
+"approved action" means concretely for Execute) — exactly the kind of
+audit-before-migrate discipline used for Hospitality's schema gate.
+
